title: Jedi Relations
subtitle: Work with the guardians of peace and justice.
is-card: true
tags: caucus_affairs
card-image: img/card_jedi.svg
view-if: jedi_timer <= 0 and cardok_jedi
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; jedi_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "jedi"
new-page: true

= Jedi Relations

The Jedi Order is the Republic's oldest institution, and its most misunderstood. Our relations with the Order are [+ jedi_relation : relationships +], and public trust in the Jedi is [+ jedi_standing : level +].

- @visit: Visit the Temple and listen.
- @hunt: Urge the Council to hunt for the Sith Master.
- @defend: Defend the Order in the Senate.
- @reform: Speak for reform of the Order.
- @anakin: Ask about young Skywalker.
- @attachment: Ask the Council to accept attachment.
- @new_order: Help the Jedi found a new Order.
- @easy_discard

@visit
view-if: jedi_relation < 85
subtitle: +6 relations with the Jedi.
on-arrival: jedi_relation += 6

The Caucus delegation leaves with no promises and a great many proverbs.

@hunt
view-if: date >= 18 and jedi_suspicion < 9 and not sidious_known
subtitle: [? if jedi_relation >= 45 : They may listen. ?][? if jedi_relation < 45 : They do not trust us enough to listen. ?]
choose-if: jedi_relation >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the Jedi are too weak.
on-arrival: jedi_suspicion += 1; jedi_relation -= 2; evidence += 0.2

The Council agrees to quietly expand its search. "The dark side clouds everything," Yoda warns. "Impossible to see, the future is."

@defend
view-if: jedi_standing < 85
subtitle: +4 public trust in the Jedi.
on-arrival: jedi_standing += 4; jedi_relation += 2; sec_relation -= 2

The Caucus reminds the Senate that the Jedi have kept the peace for a thousand years without an army.

@reform
view-if: (date >= 108 or war) and jedi_reform < 3 and not jedi_reformed
subtitle: The Order resents it, but a less rigid Order might keep its troubled Knights.
on-arrival: jedi_reform += 1; jedi_relation -= 4; anakin_fall -= 0.7; jedi_standing += 1

The Caucus argues that the Order's rules, on attachment, on the recruitment of infants, on becoming generals, belong to a calmer age. Some younger Jedi quietly agree.

@anakin
view-if: anakin_found and date >= 20 and anakin_fall > 0.5
subtitle: [? if jedi_relation >= 60 : The Council may confide in us. ?][? if jedi_relation < 60 : The Council is protective of its own. ?]
choose-if: jedi_relation >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations with the Jedi are not close enough.
on-arrival: anakin_fall -= 0.6; jedi_relation -= 1

Obi-Wan Kenobi admits he worries about his apprentice: the boy is brilliant, angry and far too fond of [+ pal_title +]'s company. The Caucus gently suggests that someone at the Temple should spend more time with him than Palpatine does.

@attachment
view-if: jedi_reform >= 3 and not jedi_reformed
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Code's rule against attachment is the one that matters most.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and jedi_relation >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: [? if jedi_relation < 60 : The Council does not trust us enough. ?][? if jedi_relation >= 60 : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: capital -= 1; jedi_reformed = 1; anakin_fall -= 1.5; jedi_relation -= 3; jedi_standing += 2

After three years of argument the Council relents: a Jedi may love, and marry, and remain a Jedi. Master Yoda is said to have laughed when the vote was taken. Master Windu is said not to have.

@new_order
view-if: jedi_reformed and anakin_light and not new_jedi_order
subtitle: −2 political capital. Families, Knights trained as adults, no more Jedi generals, an open Council.
choose-if: capital >= 2 and jedi_relation >= 70
unavailable-subtitle: [? if jedi_relation < 70 : The Council does not trust us enough. ?][? if jedi_relation >= 70 : Needs 2 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: capital -= 2; new_jedi_order = 1; jedi_standing += 10; jedi_strength += 1; jedi_relation += 5; anakin_fall = 0
achievement: new_jedi_order

The Order that emerges is smaller at first, and stranger. Its Knights may have families. It takes students who come to it as adults, by choice, not infants taken from their cribs. It will advise the Republic's armies, but it will not command them. And its Council meets in the open, with a seat for a young Knight from Tatooine whom the old Masters once feared. The holocrons call it the New Jedi Order.

